                    # AI CONTENT CREATOR & SOCIAL MEDIA SPECIALIST



Emerging Design & Leather Goods Brand | Part-Time | Remote



LIHANN GEORGE is looking for a creative and highly curious 'AI Content Creator & Social Media Specialist' to help us build and grow the visual world of our young Belgian design and leather goods brand.



LIHANN GEORGE was launched during Paris Fashion Week in January 2026.



Our world is deeply connected to 'architecture, craftsmanship, materials, art and timeless design'. Our showroom is located at the Kanaal site by Axel Vervoordt near Antwerp — an environment where architecture, interiors, art and craftsmanship naturally come together.



We are building a small international team and are looking for someone who combines two important strengths:

a strong understanding of social media + hands-on experience creating high-quality visual content using AI.



This is not a traditional Social Media Manager position.

And it is not simply an AI prompting position.

We are looking for someone who can understand a brand, develop ideas, create content and gradually take ownership of how those ideas come to life on social media.



THE ROLE

Your role will combine social media, content creation, storytelling, AI image generation and video creation.



You will work closely with the founder and potentially with another tea
mber focused on visual research, graphic design and brand assets.



We would gradually like you to take ownership of:

SOCIAL MEDIA & CONTENT

* developing weekly and monthly content plans;

* proposing original Instagram posts, Reels and Stories;

* developing recurring content concepts and storytelling formats;

* writing strong English captions;

* creating content around products, materials, craftsmanship, architecture, art, spaces and lifestyle;

* planning and scheduling content;

* creating and editing short-form video for social media;

* understanding how feed posts, Reels and Stories work together;

* identifying opportunities to create engaging content from existing brand material;

* following relevant developments in social media without blindly following trends;

* monitoring content performance and understanding what resonates;

* suggesting improvements based on analytics;

* helping us build a relevant and engaged audience;

* supporting launches, Pop-Ups, Paris showrooms and other brand 
nts through social media.



AI IMAGE & VIDEO CREATION

AI will be an important part of this role.

We want to increasingly create original visual content without depending on a traditional photoshoot for every piece of communication.



You should be comfortable working from:

* existing product photography;

* packshots;

* campaign or lifestyle photography;

* a visual brand guide;

* colours and materials;

* architectural or artistic references;

* creative direction from the founder.

And translating these into new, believable visual content.



This could include:

* creating AI-generated environments around existing products;

* developing editorial or atmospheric imagery;

* placing products naturally within architectural or lifestyle settings;

* generating visual concepts based on a brand guide;

* transforming still imagery into moving content;

* creating AI-assisted short films or Reels;

* creating movement, atmosphere and transitions from existing photography;

* combining AI-generated material with real photography or video;

* editing the final material into content suitable for Instagram.



For us, believability is extremely important.

If you work with an existing LIHANN GEORGE bag, the product should remain recognisable and credible.

Its proportions, shape, construction, leather, colour and important details should not randomly change simply because AI was used.



We are interested in AI as a creative tool — not in content that immediately feels artificial.



CREATIVE DIRECTION

LIHANN GEORGE is not simply about handbags.

The bags are part of a wider visual world.



Our communication is connected to:

* architecture and spaces;

* materials and craftsmanship;

* art and objects;

* proportion and form;

* texture;

* natural light;

* landscape and travel;

* understated lifestyle;

* timeless design.



We believe strong communication does not need to shout.

We prefer authenticity, restraint and atmosphere over content that simply tries to attract attention.

Understanding this distinction is important for this role.



WHO WE ARE LOOKING FOR

You may be a strong match if you:

* have hands-on experience with social media content creation;

* understand Instagram beyond simply posting content;

* have experience creating AI-generated or AI-assisted photography;

* have experience creating AI-generated or AI-assisted video;

* can edit short-form video and create finished Reels;

* understand visual storytelling;

* have a strong eye for composition, proportion, typography and detail;

* can translate a brand guide into consistent visual content;

* can distinguish sophisticated imagery from generic AI imagery;

* write strong English;

* understand storytelling and captions;

* are naturally curious about new AI and creative tools;

* experiment and learn independently;

* are organised enough to work with a content calendar;

* analyse what works and adjust accordingly;

* naturally bring ideas rather than waiting for detailed instructions.

Experience within fashion, design, architecture, interiors, beauty or premium/luxury brands is highly valuable.



TOOLS

We deliberately don't want to give you a checklist of AI software you must know.

AI tools develop extremely quickly.

We are much more interested in what you can create, how you think and how you choose the right tool for the result you want.



In your application, please tell us which tools are currently part of your workflow for:

* AI image generation;

* AI image editing;

* AI video generation;

* video editing;

* social media planning/publishing.



This may include tools such as ChatGPT, Midjourney, Adobe Firefly, Runway, Kling, Veo, Canva, CapCut, Adobe tools or completely different tools.



We are interested in understanding why and how you use them, not in counting how many tools you know.



HOW WE WORK

This is initially a part-time remote role of approximately 10–15 hours per week, with the possibility to grow over time.



We are a small team.

That means you will have room to influence how we work and help build systems and creative processes rather than simply stepping into an existing large marketing department.



We value:

honesty

curiosity

initiative

creativity

attention to detail

independent thinking

authenticity

continuous learning



Quality is more important to us than speed.

AI is strongly encouraged.

But AI should support human creativity and judgement — not replace them.



HOW TO APPLY

Please do not send us a long generic cover letter.

We would much rather see what you have actually created and understand how you think.



Please answer the following questions.

1. SOCIAL MEDIA EXPERIENCE

Which social media account have you personally worked on that best represents your abilities?

Please send us the link and explain exactly what you were personally responsible for.



Were you responsible for:

* strategy?

* concepts?

* captions?

* graphics?

* Reels?

* posting?

* analytics?

* growth?

Please be specific.



2. AI IMAGE PORTFOLIO

Please share 3–5 examples of AI-generated or AI-assisted images that you personally created.



For at least one example, please show us:

the original/source material ? your final result



and briefly explain:

* what you received;

* what you wanted to achieve;

* which tools you used;

* what you personally created or edited.



3. AI VIDEO PORTFOLIO

Please share at least one AI-generated or AI-assisted video that you personally created.



Explain briefly:

* the original idea;

* which tools you used;

* which parts were AI-generated;

* which parts you created or edited yourself;

* whether you produced the finished video independently.



4. PRODUCT CONSISTENCY

Imagine we give you a clean photograph of one of our handbags.

We want to place that exact bag into an architectural environment using AI.

How would you approach this while making sure the bag itself remains as accurate as possible?

We are interested in your process, not just the name of the tool you would use.



5. CONTENT OWNERSHIP

Imagine you join LIHANN GEORGE and I tell you:

“We need content for next week, but I haven't d
 what we should post.”



What would you do?

Please briefly explain how you would approach the week from idea to finished content.



6. VIDEO CREATION

If we provide you with:

* 5 product photographs;

* several architectural/inspirational images;

* a brand guide;

* and some existing video footage;

how confidently could you turn this into a finished Instagram Reel yourself?

Please explain what you could personally do from start to finish.



7. LIHANN GEORGE

Please look at our Instagram 



Imagine you joined us tomorrow.

What is one content idea you would be genuinely excited to explore for LIHANN GEORGE that we are currently not doing?



There is no correct answer.

We want to discover your creative instinct.



8. YOUR STRENGTHS

Which part of this role gives you the most energy?

And which part are you less experienced in or would still like to learn?



Please be completely honest.

Nobody needs to be perfect at everything.



Finally, please include:

* your current availability;

* preferred working hours;

* expected hourly rate;

* other ongoing jobs or clients;

* portfolio / website / relevant links.



Please start your application with the words:

FORM FOLLOWS FEELING

This lets us know you have read the complete job description.



We look forward to discovering your work, ideas and creative process.
